 "source": "# Anchors, aliases, and the merge key. The grammar gives each a distinct\n# node type (anchor / alias); `<<` is just a string_scalar key.\n\ndefaults: &def\n  host:  localhost\n  port : 8080\n\n# Alias as a whole value.\ncopy: *def\n\n# Merge key plus an override.\nprod:\n  <<:  *def\n  port:  443 # overrides the merged port\n\n# Anchor on a flow mapping. Fits at 80, breaks at 40 -- prettier keeps\n# the anchor on the key and breaks the mapping, it does not convert to block.\npair: &p {host: alpha.example.com,port: 8080}\n\n# Alias of that flow mapping.\nagain: *p\n\n# Two anchors in one document, used together.\neast: &east {region: us-east-1, role: primary}\nwest: &west {region: us-west-2,role: replica}\nregions: [*east,*west]\n",
